{'symbol': 'ABBV', 'date': '2021-07-21 01:00:00', 'title': 'VENETOCLAX (VENCLEXTA®) GRANTED US FDA BREAKTHROUGH THERAPY DESIGNATION (BTD) IN HIGHER RISK MYELODYSPLASTIC SYNDROME (MDS)', 'text': 'NORTH CHICAGO, ILL., JULY 21, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0ABBVIE (NYSE: ABBV) ANNOUNCED TODAY THAT THE U.S. FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION (FDA) GRANTED A BREAKTHROUGH THERAPY DESIGNATION (BTD) TO VENETOCLAX (VENCLEXTA®) IN COMBINATION WITH AZACITIDINE FOR THE POTENTIAL TREATMENT OF ADULT PATIENTS WITH PREVIOUSLY UNTREATED INTERMEDIATE-, HIGH- AND VERY HIGH-RISK MYELODYSPLASTIC SYNDROMES (MDS) BASED ON REVISED INTERNATIONAL PROGNOSTIC SCORING SYSTEM (IPSS-R).'}